      "id": "8d0be7b9-a01d-42c1-bb4c-8c59893a3944",
      "text": "Time is absolute and comes in discrete ticks, one executed state per tick. A moving clock ticks slower than absolute time, by $(c - v)/c$ for a source moving at $v$, a slowdown the model ties to inertia.",
